# Q1. Explain the Java Memory Model (JMM).

### What they are testing

* Thread safety
* Concurrency
* JVM knowledge

---

## Excellent Answer

> The Java Memory Model defines how threads interact with memory and guarantees visibility, ordering, and atomicity.
>
> Every thread has its own working memory, while objects reside in the heap.
>
> Without proper synchronization, one thread may not immediately observe changes made by another thread.
>
> Java provides mechanisms like `volatile`, `synchronized`, and classes from `java.util.concurrent` to establish happens-before relationships and ensure correct visibility between threads.

---

